# Trivy vulnerability ignore list.
#
# Only add entries here when a fix is not yet available from the upstream
# distro (i.e. Trivy reports "fixed" against an upstream version string that
# has not actually been published as an installable apk/deb package yet), or
# when a finding is a confirmed false positive / accepted risk. Always
# include a comment with the reasoning and an `exp:` expiry so stale
# suppressions get re-evaluated instead of silently accumulating forever.
#
# CVE-2026-14456 / CVE-2026-45447 (OpenSSL, libcrypto3/libssl3 in the
# node:20-alpine base image): Trivy's vulnerability DB lists fixed versions
# (3.5.7-r0 / 3.5.8-r0), but as of this writing Alpine's 3.23 apk repository
# has not yet published a build containing them - `apk upgrade` cannot
# resolve to a fixed package today. Re-check on each Dependabot Docker base
# image bump; remove these lines once `trivy image node:20-alpine` no longer
# reports them.
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-45447 exp:2026-12-31
